course: dictionary
lesson: 9226
title: Sometime and a time not named
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Sometime means at a time that is not said exactly. «Wanna play online sometime?» means the speaker wants a game, but no day or hour is chosen yet.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Betelgeuse will explode as a supernova sometime within about the next 100,000 years; nobody can say exactly when.» The words nobody can say exactly when show that sometime means a time that is not fixed.
explain: A good check is to swap in a phrase like at some point. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right. As an adjective, sometime means former, as in his sometime teacher, but this use is rare.
fact: Sometime means at a time that is not said exactly.
fact: «Come and visit sometime» means come one day, when it suits you, but no date is named.
fact: Sometime is an adverb in most sentences. The adjective meaning former, as in his sometime teacher, is rare.
fact: In the Betelgeuse sentence, sometime points to a time about 100,000 years away, and nobody knows the exact day.
fact: Do not mix up sometime with sometimes, which means now and then, or with some time, which means a period of time.
exercise: «Wanna play online sometime?» What does sometime mean here? | *At some time not decided yet | Only in the morning | At exactly 3 o'clock today | Never, not ever
exercise: Betelgeuse «will explode as a supernova sometime within about the next 100,000 years; nobody can say exactly when.» Why can nobody name the day? | Because the star is too bright to see | Because the star has already exploded | *Because the time is not fixed exactly | Because nobody owns a telescope
exercise: Which phrase could replace sometime in «Come and visit sometime»? | at 9 o'clock tomorrow | last week | *one day, when it suits you | never ever
test: «Let's meet sometime next week.» What does sometime mean here? | *At a time in next week that is not yet chosen | Never | Exactly on Monday at noon | Four days ago
test: What word could replace sometime in «I will tidy my room sometime»? | *at some point, at a time not named | very quickly | at exactly noon | only in the past
exam: Which sentence uses sometime to mean former? | Come and see us sometime. | It will happen sometime, nobody knows when. | *She met his sometime teacher at the shop. | He sometimes runs to school.
